========================================================================================
UNIVERSITY RECRUITMENT HIERARCHY & WORKFLOW
========================================================================================

Stage 1: DEPARTMENT REQUISITION (Deans & Directors)
  - Dean or Director raises a new hiring requirement for their faculty/department.
  - Submits cadre type (Teaching / Non-Teaching), positions, workload justification, qualifications, and budget.
  - Action: "Submit to Dean Academic".
  - Visibility: At this stage, only Dean Academic and HR see that an application was submitted; VC/Registrar does NOT see it yet.

Stage 2: ACADEMIC SCRUTINY (Dean Academic)
  - Dean Academic reviews the teaching load, student-faculty ratio, and UGC/AICTE compliance.
  - Actions:
      1) Approve & Forward to VC / Registrar for executive & financial sanction.
      2) Return for Clarification (with query remarks to Dean).
      3) Reject Requisition.

Stage 3: EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE SANCTION (VC / Registrar)
  - Once approved by Dean Academic, the requisition lands on the VC / Registrar desk.
  - Reviews institutional priority, post clearance, and sanction budget.
  - Action: Grant Executive Sanction & Forward to HR Directorate.

Stage 4: ACTIVE SOURCING & JOB POSTING (HR Department)
  - HR receives the sanctioned requisition.
  - Posts the job opening on official channels: Indeed, LinkedIn, Newspapers, University Website, etc.
  - Tracks advertisement spend per channel.
  - Uploads received candidate resumes and applicant profiles.

Stage 5: INTERVIEW PANEL & SELECTION (HR Department & Selection Committee)
  - HR schedules interviews with panel members (panel names, interview date, venue/mode).
  - Panel conducts interviews, scores candidates (subject knowledge, research, teaching aptitude, communication).
  - Recommends selected candidates, issues offer letters, verifies documents, and completes joining.

